{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And answered</b> — The meaning is: Israel who bring a sin-offering for their inadvertent sins are presumptuously guilty in severe matters, for they are grave, yet they were not mindful of them and bring an offering for something concealed, while they act improperly with presumptuous intent; also the priests in the matter of purity and impurity. Therefore Haggai said: \"So is this people\" — these are the priests; \"and so is this nation\" — these are Israel; \"and so every work of their hands.\"" "<b>And that they offer</b> — on the altar before Me, and this is the meaning of \"it is unclean.\" Now it is clarified that holiness has no power to sanctify what was not holy by means of intermediary contact, unlike the power of a defiling thing to defile. And this was by way of parable, like the way of Nathan to David, who seized him with his words and said to him: \"You are the man.\" And it is also fitting for this to be a parable, because they build houses for their dwellings while the House of HaShem lies ruined; therefore [comes] what follows it."], :book :haggai, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "The phrase 'also the priests' interrupts the syntax of the first comment; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Haggai" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"] ["Ibn Ezra on Haggai -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:34.026503805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}